cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Quantum Reinforcement Learning: generalizzare con pochi ambienti di training"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Caponnetto"
    given-names: "Angelo"
    affiliation: "Università degli Studi di Firenze"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ImAngw/vqc-thesis"
abstract: "Study of a reinforcement-learning policy whose action head is a variational quantum circuit, on partially observable 2D grid navigation. With few training layouts (K=25) the quantum head generalises better than a classical MLP of the same size, also at equal entropy; a classical head with Fourier features matches it, so the advantage is a Fourier-type inductive bias. Under calibrated IBM noise (Torino, Brisbane) the loss in return is small."
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - variational quantum circuits
  - generalization
  - quantum machine learning

preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: "Quantum Reinforcement Learning: generalizzare con pochi ambienti di training"
